    "q-348519": {
      "dom_id": "step-q348519",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}+6x+9}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{{x}^{2}+6x+9}=\\frac{x+1}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+3)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+3)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\nx+1=A(x+3)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+1 & =A(-3+3)+B \\\\ B & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+1 & =A(0+3)-2 \\\\ 1 & =3A-2 \\\\ A & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{(x+3)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{2}{(x+3)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x+1}{(x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{x+3}-\\frac{2}{(x+3)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)+2(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})+2(-\\frac{1}{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
